# radiomics_dispersion_pipeline

## approach1 package layout

The SecureGPT few-shot dispersion/relapse pipeline is implemented as the `approach1/` Python package. [`approach1.py`](approach1.py) is a thin CLI wrapper that re-exports the original module API for backward compatibility.

```
pipeline/
├── approach1.py          # CLI entry: python approach1.py ...
├── approach1/              # implementation package
│   ├── config.py
│   ├── models.py
│   ├── data.py
│   ├── splits.py
│   ├── prompts/
│   ├── schema/
│   ├── api/
│   ├── checkpoint/
│   ├── evaluation/
│   ├── inference.py
│   ├── orchestration.py
│   └── cli.py
└── tests/approach1/
```

## Run

```bash
cd pipeline
python3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
python approach1.py --csv-path /path/to/cases.csv --outdir ./outputs -y
```

## Tests

```bash
pytest tests/approach1/ -v
```
